## Failover Procedures

### Automated Failover

| Component | Trigger | Action | Time |
|-----------|---------|--------|------|
| Load Balancer | Health check fail | Route to healthy AZ | 30 sec |
| Database | Primary failure | Promote replica | 2 min |
| Cache | Node failure | Failover node | 1 min |
| DNS | Region health | Route53 failover | 1 min |

### Manual Failover (Region)

| Step | Action | Owner | Time |
|------|--------|-------|------|
| 1 | Declare disaster | IC | 5 min |
| 2 | Notify stakeholders | Comms | 10 min |
| 3 | Verify DR readiness | SRE | 15 min |
| 4 | Execute DNS failover | SRE | 5 min |
| 5 | Verify data sync | DBA | 15 min |
| 6 | Promote DR database | DBA | 15 min |
| 7 | Scale DR compute | SRE | 20 min |
| 8 | Verify services | QA | 30 min |
| 9 | Customer notification | Comms | 10 min |
| 10 | Monitor stability | SRE | Ongoing |
| **Total** | — | — | **~2 hours** |

